body.en:
def balanced(s):
    pairs = {")": "(", "]": "[", "}": "{"}
    stack = []
    for ch in s:
        if ch in "([{": stack.append(ch)
        elif ch in pairs:
            if not stack or stack.pop() != pairs[ch]: return False
    return not stack
It is O(n): each character is pushed and popped at most once. The final "return not stack" catches leftover openers like "((". Compilers, JSON parsers and calculators that respect brackets all build on this idea.

